  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday Night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1034 AM CDT Tue Aug 11 2026\n\nDuring the latter half of the week, high pressure will continue \nto build north, and temperatures will only get hotter. High \ntemperatures will get into the upper-90s for many locations west \nof the Plateau Thursday into Saturday, and then we may even be \ntalking about triple digit heat by Sunday. At Nashville, the NBM \ngives an 80% chance of hitting 100 degrees Sunday. Even if we \ndon't hit triple digits, this heat wave will still be dangerous. \nThis prolonged stretch of hot temperatures will make for major to \nextreme heat risk for all. So be sure to take care of yourself and\ncheck on others who may be more sensitive to heat. Unfortunately,\novernight won't offer much relief with lows in the mid to \nupper-70s with high humidity.\n\nAs far as rain goes, the more this high pressure builds overhead, \nthe more rain chances go down. There are low rain chances Thursday & \nFriday, but the weekend looks to be dry which coincides with the \nhottest temperatures. The heat should break early next week as \nthe high moves west and a boundary comes down from the north.",
